-- Classic 1.60: the spawns of the vanilla world events (VMaNGOS creature, creature_addon and gameobject, development database
-- snapshot 2026-09-28), which the world baseline left out. Guids are the VMaNGOS guids + 20,000,000 (creatures) / + 30,000,000
-- (gameobjects), the same offsets as the rest of the converted world. A negative event entry hides a normal spawn while the
-- event runs (those rows already exist and only get the game_event row). A VMaNGOS spawn that rolls one of several entries
-- keeps its first entry. equipment_id is TrinityCore's set index (1 = the entry's first creature_equip_template set, 0 = none), never a
-- VMaNGOS equipment id. Templates come from the retail base (vanilla ids are still there); a spawn whose template is missing
-- is skipped by the loader with a log line, so the entries not in the converted vanilla template set are listed for a check:
